It&#39;s real and I&#39;ve done similar but not to that extreme. &nbsp; &nbsp;In his case get Twist the Ether on AZ and he needs Isothermic Transducer. &nbsp; Hit AZ with fire damage, then keep hitting yourself with fire damage through Twist the Ether until you hit a number you like, and then hit the villain. &nbsp;

[/quote]

Wait, how does that work? Usually you can&#39;t select the same target multiple times for the same effect. Does that reset every time AZ hits himself with fire damage? That&#39;s ridiculous.

And if AZ has a billion and change damage on him, how did the villain end up dying with zero hp?&nbsp;

[quote="Powerhound_2000"]

Isothermic Transducer reacts every time AZ is dealt fire damage and he can choose any target with the new instance of damage including himself. For the victory screen will it always show zero HP on the final screen for the villain if they were defeated no matter how much damage was inflicted. &nbsp;

[/quote]

My only other question: Presumably, that shouldn&#39;t increase exponentially, only by the amount of damage boosters you have in play. To get to a billion+ damage . . . how long did this person have to sit there and click? That&#39;s bizarre.&nbsp;

Yeah, doing it the simple way just bouncing the damage with Twist the Ether and a few damage boosters will take you a very long time. &nbsp;But with proper application of Coolant Blast and Dynamic Syphon, it&#39;s possible to grow your damage exponentially. &nbsp;Full details [url=https://greaterthangames.com/comment/143246#comment-143246]here[/url]. &nbsp;I&#39;m very proud of these screenshots.

